#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:26
msgid "I have to include index.php in my URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:28
msgid ""
"If a URL like ``/mypage/find/apple`` doesn't work, but the similar URL "
"``/index.php/mypage/find/apple`` does, that sounds like your "
"**.htaccess** rules (for Apache) are not set up properly, or the "
"``mod_rewrite`` extension in Apache's **httpd.conf** is commented out. "
"See :ref:`urls-remove-index-php`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:35
msgid "Only the default page loads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:37
msgid ""
"If you find that no matter what you put in your URL only your default "
"page is loading, it might be that your server does not support the "
"REQUEST_URI variable needed to serve search-engine friendly URLs. As a "
"first step, open your **app/Config/App.php** file and look for the URI "
"Protocol information. It will recommend that you try a couple of "
"alternate settings. If it still doesn't work after you've tried this "
"you'll need to force CodeIgniter to add a question mark (``?``) to your "
"URLs. To do this open your **app/Config/App.php** file and change this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:48
msgid "To this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:53
msgid "No input file specified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:55
msgid ""
"If you see \"No input file specified\", try to change the rewrite rule "
"like the following (to add ``?`` after ``index.php``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:62
msgid "My app works fine locally but not on the production server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:64
msgid "Make sure that the case of the folder and file names matches the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:66
msgid ""
"Many developers develop on case-insensitive file systems on Windows or "
"macOS. However, most server environments use case-sensitive file systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:69
msgid ""
"For example, when you have **app/Controllers/Product.php**, you must use "
"``Product`` as the short classname, not ``product``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:72
msgid "If the file name case is incorrect, the file is not found on the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:75
msgid "The tutorial gives 404 errors everywhere :("
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:77
msgid ""
"You can't follow the tutorial using PHP's built-in web server. It doesn't"
" process the **.htaccess** file needed to route requests properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:81
msgid ""
"The solution: use Apache to serve your site, or else the built-in "
"CodeIgniter equivalent, ``php spark serve`` from your project root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:87
msgid "What's with an unhelpful \"Whoops!\" page?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:89
msgid ""
"You find that your app is displaying a page with \"Whoops!\" and then the"
" text line \"We seem to have hit a snag. Please try again later...\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:92
msgid ""
"That is a sign that you are in production mode and have hit an "
"unrecoverable error, which we don't want to show to the viewer of the "
"webapp, for better security."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:96
msgid ""
"You can see the error in the log file. See `CodeIgniter Error Logs`_ "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/troubleshooting.rst:98
msgid ""
"If you reach this page while developing you should change your "
"environment to \"development\" (in **.env**). See :ref:`setting-"
"development-mode` for more details. After that, reload the page. You will"
" see the error and the back trace."
msgstr ""

